IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mlsfb-surcharge`

-- A New Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge--Fringe Benefits) Act 1999 (Cth) -- worked cases from the seat of the taxpayer
-- without hospital cover who receives reportable fringe benefits: ss 4, 6, 7, 10-16.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case or an ATO publication. Fixtures are generated by scratchpad
-- gen_a-new-tax-system-medicare-levy-surcharge-fringe-benefits-act-1999_baseline.py; expected results were written by hand from
-- the deposited text.
--
-- Tier thresholds: every fixture uses $90,000 / $105,000 / $140,000 (family: double, $180,000 / $210,000 / $280,000), the
-- Private Health Insurance Act s 22-35 figures "for the 2021-22 and 2022-23 financial year", as ASSUMED stand-ins for the indexed
-- figures (not deposited). The s 22-40(4) increase for two or more children is a formula the deposit drops; fixtures use 0.
--
-- The life (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe): chloe c073 (2034-04-01), "Turns 31; hospital cover taken out
-- before 1 July to avoid the loading". The scenario states she married Liam (Kings Park), that Oliver (3) and Ella (0) are their
-- children, and that from February 2034 she earns $110,000 at Jarrah Legal Technologies. It does NOT state her reportable
-- fringe benefits total, Liam's income, or the day the cover began. ASSUMED: cover (a family policy that counts under s 4) from
-- 1 April 2034, the event date, so 274 days uncovered in 2033-34 (1 July 2033 to 31 March 2034); income for surcharge purposes
-- $110,000; reportable fringe benefits total $3,000; Liam's income for surcharge purposes $60,000 (and $80,000 in a variant).

